  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency protection and assistance to refugees in transit/reception centers and receiving settlements in Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This UNHCR project provides emergency protection services and assistance for refugees in transit/reception centers and receiving settlements in Uganda. UNHCR  with its Implementing Partners will reinforce protection services for people at heightened risk of GBV and GBV survivors as well as provide health services. This project targets 800,000 affected people, 144,000  men,192,000 women, and 464,000 children including 33,000 Persons with Disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
